{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___. I’m Dr. ___. You’re here today for your scheduled IVIG infusion, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:22:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. This is my fourth one. But I’ve been getting them in the hospital because of reactions I’ve had before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:23:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I see from your history. You’ve had some chest tightness and high blood pressure after past infusions. We’ll monitor you closely today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I actually had some sweating and squeezing chest pain this morning—about a 4 out of 10. Felt faint and nauseous too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:25:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you said it’s similar to how you feel when you’re dehydrated?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:26:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Exactly. I get that a lot because of my mitochondrial disease. But I wanted to mention it just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:27:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. We’ll keep an eye on your vitals. We’re going to start you on a saline infusion first—1900cc over several hours—to help with fluid balance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:28:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s what I usually get at home. Every week or so, I get IV fluids for my orthostatic hypotension."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:29:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and it’s especially important today before the IVIG. We want to minimize any side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:30:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. Oh, and I’ve been meaning to mention—I’ve got this rash on my left lower leg. It’s been growing for about a month."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:31:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Let me take a look."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see a red, slightly raised patch with scaling. It’s well-defined but irregular. You said it’s itchy and crusts over?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:34:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. It feels like the squamous cell carcinoma I had removed a few years ago. I also have these tumors in my thigh I see the orthopedic oncologist for."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:35:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history, we should have your dermatologist evaluate this. It may be eczema, but we don’t want to miss anything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2186-02-20 14:36:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. I’ll make sure to bring it up at my next appointment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2186-02-20 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your saline infusion is halfway done. How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2186-02-20 18:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A bit better. The chest tightness has eased. Still a little lightheaded when I sit up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2186-02-20 18:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected with your autonomic dysfunction. We’ll keep monitoring. We’ll finish the fluids tonight and give IVIG tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2186-02-21 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re going to prep for your IVIG today. First, we’ll check your labs, including your IgG levels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2186-02-21 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Are those the immune protein levels?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2186-02-21 08:02:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your IgG subclasses 1 and 3 are a bit low, which confirms you still need the IVIG. We’ll give you 15 grams today—half your usual dose, but more frequently now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2186-02-21 08:03:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, switching to every two weeks instead of monthly. I hope that helps with side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2186-02-21 08:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the goal. We’ll also pre-medicate you with Benadryl and Tylenol to reduce reaction risk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2186-02-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting the IVIG now. We’ll go slowly and check your vitals every 15 minutes at first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2186-02-21 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doc, I’m starting to feel that chest tightness again. And short of breath. A little nauseous too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2186-02-21 10:31:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, let’s slow the infusion. We’ll get an EKG and check your blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2186-02-21 10:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your EKG looks stable—no signs of heart strain. Blood pressure is 151/96, a bit high but not alarming. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2186-02-21 10:46:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is this dangerous? Could it be my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2186-02-21 10:47:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your troponin levels—those are heart damage markers—and they’re normal. This seems like a reaction to the IVIG, not a heart issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2186-02-21 10:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like what I’ve had before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2186-02-21 10:50:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, very similar. We’ll continue at a slower rate and watch you closely. The symptoms should improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2186-02-21 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing better. The chest tightness has eased, and your breathing is normal. We finished the IVIG."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2186-02-21 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel more like myself. Still a mild headache, but nothing like earlier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2186-02-21 14:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. We’ll keep you overnight for observation, as usual, and plan to discharge tomorrow if you stay stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your repeat labs are normal. Troponins stayed negative, and your blood count is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No more chest pain or nausea. Headache’s gone too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. Your physical exam is also improved—abdomen is no longer tender, and your skin lesion looks unchanged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We recommend you follow up with your dermatologist about that leg rash, given your history of skin cancer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:05:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And my IVIG schedule—every two weeks—is still on track?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. And no changes to your other medications. You’re cleared to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:07:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Thanks for watching me so closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. If you develop severe headache, chest pain, or trouble breathing at home, go to the ER. Otherwise, keep your follow-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:10:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll call my team if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:11:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well with the IVIG overall—more strength, you said?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:12:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I feel stronger than before I started. Worth the side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the goal. We’ll keep supporting you through these infusions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:15:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it. I’ll see you in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2186-02-22 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. ___. Safe travels home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2186-02-20 14:21:00",
    "admission_end": "2186-02-22 12:05:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with a history of mitochondrial myopathy, coronary artery disease, and hypogammaglobulinemia was admitted for a scheduled IVIG infusion, now adjusted to a half-dose every two weeks. Upon admission, he reported baseline symptoms of chest tightness, diaphoresis, nausea, and lightheadedness, which he associates with dehydration due to autonomic dysfunction. He received a 1900cc saline infusion overnight to optimize fluid status. The next day, he was pre-medicated and received 15g of IVIG, after which he developed transient chest tightness, shortness of breath, nausea, and headache—consistent with prior infusion reactions. Serial troponins and EKGs showed no evidence of cardiac ischemia. Symptoms resolved by the following morning. A chronic skin lesion on the left lower extremity, growing over the past month and reminiscent of prior squamous cell carcinoma, was noted, and dermatology follow-up was recommended. The patient remained stable, and no medication changes were made. He was discharged home in good condition with plans to continue outpatient IVIG and follow-up with specialists.",
    "problems": [
      "Hypogammaglobulinemia, unspecified",
      "Disorders of mitochondrial metabolism",
      "Symptomatic inflammatory myopathy in diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of native coronary artery",
      "Other and unspecified angina pectoris",
      "Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty status",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Nausea alone",
      "Shortness of breath",
      "Headache",
      "Unspecified disorder of skin and subcutaneous tissue",
      "Personal history of other malignant neoplasm of skin",
      "Personal history of sudden cardiac arrest"
    ]
  }
}
